  "content": "# Weekly Pipeline Report — Leadership\n*Draft · All figures sourced from workspace records · Week of Sep 1, 2026*\n\n---\n\n## Pipeline Snapshot\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Total active pipeline | **$288,000** across 8 deals |\n| Closing in September | **$127,000** (4 deals) |\n| September at-risk | **$94,000** — Corvus + Beacon |\n| September low-risk | **$33,000** — Northwind + Radley |\n\n**Owner split:** Pat — $154K (Northwind, Beacon, Summit, Meridian) · Alex — $134K (Corvus, Radley, Harbor & Finch, Atlas)\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL — Act This Week\n\n### Corvus Media — Renewal Save · $32K · Closes Sep 20\nChampion departed July; usage is down 40%. Renewal is 2 weeks out with no internal sponsor. An exec-to-exec call must happen before end of week — without a new sponsor this deal is lost. **Owner: Alex.**\n\n### Beacon Health — Expansion + Renewal · $62K expansion / $124K ARR · Closes Sep 26\nProposal review call is Thursday. Procurement is blocking on a usage review before they'll approve the combined expansion + renewal. Usage report must be ready before that call. Missing Thursday likely pushes both the $62K expansion and the October renewal. **Owner: Pat.**\n\n---\n\n## Watch Closely\n\n### Northwind Logistics — Warehouse Team #3 · $24K · Closes Sep 12\nIn negotiation, low risk. Terms are nearly agreed — the only remaining step is sending the multi-team pricing addendum. Should close this week. **Owner: Pat.**\n\n### Radley Manufacturing — Reporting Add-On · $9K · Closes Sep 30\nCFO-driven, low risk. Needs a one-page ROI summary. Clean and closeable. **Owner: Alex.**\n\n### Harbor & Finch — New Business · $38K · Closes Oct 15\nTwo strong discovery calls, decision maker engaged. Security review is the long pole — could add 3–4 weeks and slip the Oct 15 close. Security questionnaire needs to go back immediately. **Owner: Alex.**\n\n### Summit Facilities — Second Department · $41K · Closes Nov 5\nPilot went well; expansion scoped to maintenance division. **Risk: budget cycle opens Oct 1 — missing that window means a quarter delay.** Scope workshop with maintenance leadership must happen before Oct 1. **Owner: Pat.**\n\n### Atlas Field Services — New Business · $55K · Closes Oct 31\nCompeting against an incumbent spreadsheet process. Reference call with Northwind ops lead is the next step — proof from a similar customer is the deciding factor. **Owner: Alex.**\n\n### Meridian Dental — New Business · $27K · Closes Nov 20\nNo response in 9 days since pricing was shared. Silence post-pricing is a warning sign; needs a follow-up this week. **Owner: Pat.**\n\n---\n\n## Pipeline by Stage\n\n| Stage | Deals | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| Negotiation | 1 | $24,000 |\n| Proposal | 2 | $71,000 |\n| Evaluation | 3 | $134,000 |\n| Discovery | 2 | $59,000 |\n\n---\n\n## Account Health\n\n| Account | ARR | Renewal | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Corvus Media | $32K | Sep 20 | **At risk** — no sponsor, usage −40% |\n| Beacon Health | $124K | Oct 30 | **Watch** — procurement gate on usage review |\n| Northwind Logistics | $86K | Jan 15 | Healthy — expanding |\n| Summit Facilities | $58K | Feb 10 | Healthy — expanding |\n| Radley Manufacturing | $47K | Mar 1 | Healthy — sticky |\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Actions\n\n1. **Alex → Corvus exec call this week.** No sponsor = no renewal. Highest-urgency item in the book.\n2. **Pat → Beacon usage report ready before Thursday.** $186K combined ARR + expansion is on the line.\n3. **Pat → Send Northwind pricing addendum today.** Deal is done; just needs the paperwork.\n4. **Pat → Book Summit scope workshop before Oct 1** to avoid a quarter slip on $41K.\n5. **Alex → Return Harbor & Finch security questionnaire** to protect the Oct 15 close.\n6. **Alex → Schedule Atlas reference call with Northwind ops lead** — that's the proof point that wins this deal.\n7. **Pat → Re-engage Meridian Dental** — 9 days of silence post-pricing needs a nudge.\n"
}"}
